        "abstract": "Wireless power transfer (WPT) has emerged as a prime scheme for replenishing electrical energy during the automated operations of intelligent devices such as drones and inspection vehicles. However, due to the unfixed parking position of the equipment to be charged, offsets between couplers are inevitable. This leads to a reduction in charging efficiency, and an extension of charging time. To improve the omnidirectional misalignment tolerance of the couplers, the multi-layer mutual compensation couplers are designed in this paper. The magnetic field strength inside the couplers is enhanced by the design scheme, thereby increasing transmission efficiency and distance. Simultaneously, uniform magnetic field within the couplers area is ensured, which enhances the omnidirectional misalignment tolerance. It can be demonstrated from the experimental results that under a longitudinal spacing of 400 mm, transmission efficiency can reach 87.25%, with efficiency fluctuation before and after complete offset not exceeding ±5%.",
