        "abstract": "The equivalence of multiple working volumes (WV) are investigated in this work by the regime of state-of-the- art sensitivity analysis (SA) techniques. To this end, surrogate modeling was utilized to efficiently calculate the Sobol’ indices as a measure of uncertainty quantification (UQ). This approach helps to appraise the contributions of different configuration parameters in the frequency range close to the lowest usable frequency (LUF), where well-stirred conditions are not met, yielding a proficient apparatus to ease the measurement process of parallelized radiated immunity (RI) tests.",
