        "abstract": "In this paper, two anisotropic thermal modeling approaches based on finite element (FE) and thermal equivalent circuit (TEC) are proposed and their performance are investigated, considering anisotropic thermal conductivity and bent geometry of a racetrack foil coil. Position-dependent thermal conductivity for the bent part of the racetrack has been applied. Three-dimensional (3-D) heat conduction partial differential equations (PDEs) in both Cartesian and cylindrical coordinate systems are solved to determine the equivalent thermal resistances considering anisotropy. The results from the proposed approaches are compared with a multi-layer FE model and a homogenization FE model, exhibiting significant advantages in accounting for the temperature gradient across different materials and simplifying the pre-modeling process.",
