        "abstract": "3D calculation and analysis for ion flow field is necessary to the residential houses adjacent to HVDC transmission lines. The building corner is traditionally modeled as absolute sharp angle and the infinite curvature leads to the singularity problem. Because the infinite curvature is impossible in reality, a rounded corner model is applied and compared with the sharp corner in this paper. The electric field calculation results at rounded corners no longer diverge as the mesh resolution increases. By comparing the electric field near corners, approximated sharp corner modeling is found to cause calculation error, and the relationship between error range and corner radius is found. In engineering applications, the calculation error with some distance from the corner is discussed.",
